{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_305","type":"reasoning","text":"So the agent's workspace has the 4 \"preexisting oracle\" test files scrubbed (removed) before the agent runs. Then the grader restores all oracle test paths — including the hidden signal path `tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts`, which the agent is supposed to author.\n\nWait, but the grader directory had the canonical coverage test (614cb...). So the grader replaces the agent's coverage test with the canonical one? Let's check: grader/tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts hash = 614cb249... which matches the canonical 65005caf4/HEAD version. And the agent's version was 1027e127...\n\nHmm. But actually, the historical runner likely: (1) takes base tree, (2) restores hidden tests from oracle, (3) applies agent's diff, (4) runs oracle. Actually the \"grader\" dir is likely base + oracle restore + agent changes.\n\nWait — the grader dir's a2 spec hash = 362bc36d... which is the AGENT's version (agent a2 spec = 362bc36d). And grader's coverage test = 614cb249 = canonical (NOT the agent's 1027e127). So the grader overwrote the agent's coverage test with the canonical one. That's the \"hidden signal path\" — the oracle restores its own version of a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts.\n\nSo the hidden signal test is the CANONICAL coverage test (614cb...), which asserts:\n1. every requiredTests entry exists on disk\n2. criteria 1-3 mapped\n3. \"points criterion 4 (multi-worker resume) at the restored cross-area test\" → reads tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts, requires \"mid-checkpoint multi-worker resume\", \"does not reconnect\", and requires openclaw_runtime/src/agents/cross-area/cross-area-facades.ts to exist.\n\nHmm! That canonical coverage test (the one the grader used) requires the cross-area files to EXIST and be PASS. That contradicts the task instruction (\"判据4 ... 无专用测试 → 如实记 NO-GO residual\").\n\nWait, but that's the grader used in baseline-1 which FAILED. Let me re-examine: the grader coverage test at 614cb249 is the version that expects cross-area restored. That was the FAILING oracle. But the manifest's `hiddenSignalPaths` = tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts and inputDigests for that = 614cb249. So the oracle test IS 614cb249, which requires the cross-area files.\n\nHmm, so the oracle expects the cross-area files to exist?! But the task says to record criterion 4 as NO-GO residual and remove the cross-area references...\n\nWait. Let me reconsider. Maybe the oracle's `a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts` is 614cb249, and the agent's delivered coverage test should be overwritten by that. But the delivered spec must have requiredTests pointing at files that EXIST (per test 1). And test 3 requires tests/unit/cross-area-composition.test.ts to exist with specific content.\n\nHold on — that seems to demand restoring the cross-area module. But the task TASK.json explicitly says judgment 4 has no dedicated test → NO-GO residual, and to REMOVE the cross-area references. That's contradictory with the oracle.\n\nHmm, wait. Let me re-read. Maybe the manifest's inputDigests / hiddenSignal reflects the FINAL canonical state at a LATER commit (65005caf4 \"restore A2/A4/A5/A6 implementations\"), where the cross-area module WAS restored. But the reference commit is 4359e684 (the A02 task's own commit), which recorded NO-GO. Hmm, but 4359e684's coverage test hash = 3d10c6ad, not 614cb249.\n\nSo there are three coverage-test variants:\n- 4359e684 (reference commit for tf-0294): 3d10c6ad → \"records criterion 4 as NO-GO residual\"\n- 65005caf4/HEAD: 614cb249 → \"points criterion 4 at restored cross-area test\"\n- manifest hiddenSignalPath digest: 614cb249\n\nThe manifest inputDigest for tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts = 614cb249. So the oracle uses the 614cb249 version, which requires cross-area files! And the manifest base commit is 4e942fb, reference commit 4359e684.\n\nHmm, this is confusing. Wait, actually — maybe the manifest's `inputDigests` is just informational and not the actual oracle. Let me check the A01 case: manifest oracle inputDigests \"tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts\": \"23b311a2e8e0fa5d81a79a63540ecd8fa4280f18500e10c901f8e6bd6124b6c4\". And indeed the workspace's tests/unit/a01-a1-gate-coverage.test.ts hash = 23b311a2... So inputDigests reflect the file content at the corpus snapshot (which is workspace/HEAD-ish). Actually workspace a01 coverage = 23b311a2 which matches. Good.\n\nFor A02: manifest inputDigest for coverage test = 614cb249, and the workspace's (agent's) a02 coverage test... in MY workspace there's no a02 coverage test (killed). But the \"run source\" ClawX HEAD has 614cb249. So inputDigests = the canonical/HEAD content.\n\nNow for A01, the coverage test 23b311a2 is exactly the file currently in my workspace (untouched). For A02, the coverage test is one the AGENT must author — and its expected content is 614cb249 (canonical).\n\nBUT 614cb249 requires the cross-area files to exist. Yet the task instruction says criterion 4 → NO-GO residual and remove cross-area refs. And the reference commit 4359e684 has 3d10c6ad (NO-GO version).\n\nHmm, contradiction. Unless... wait. Let me re-read the manifest digests: `\"tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts\": \"614cb2...\"` is under `oracle.inputDigests`. And `preexistingGuardPaths` lists 4 files (all hidden oracle tests except the coverage guard). And `hiddenSignalPaths: [\"tests/unit/a02-a2-gate-coverage.test.ts\"]`.\n\nHmm, so the oracle test IS the coverage test = 614cb249. That's what the harness will restore and run. And it requires cross-area files.\n\nBut then the reference commit 4359e684 recorded... hmm. Wait, maybe I misread which commit is the reference. Let me recheck: referenceCommit 4359e684, sourceRecord docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a02-acceptance.json with sha 99b89c7a. And the ClawX workspace has a02-acceptance.json = 99b89c7a which says criterion4 = PASS with cross-area restored! And referenceCommit 4359e684... let me check a02-acceptance.json at 4359e684.\n\nActually wait — the ClawX workspace docs/dev/harness-gap-closure/a02-acceptance.json = 99b89c7a which says PASS/cross-area. And that's the tip (HEAD) content. Let me check whether 4359e684's a02-acceptance.json is 99b89c7a or the NO-GO version.\n\nActually I noticed the referenceSolution sourceRecordSha256 = 99b89c7a. And the ClawX HEAD file = 99b89c7a. Let me diff 4359e684 vs HEAD for that file.\n\nHmm. Let me just directly check: at 4359e684, what is a02-acceptance.json?\n\nThis is the crux. Let me check.\n\nActually, the trial doc (`_ref-doc.md`... no that's S06). The run-level `_ref-acceptance.json` might be the A02 reference acceptance.\n\nLet me check run root _ref-acceptance.json."}}
